    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nWhen mini.animate is active, some macros may break if they use the cursor as context. I found this to happen especially if I use search in a macro with \"/\".\r\n\r\nThis might be difficult to fix, however it would be nicht to just temporarily deactivate animation while running a macro. It would be ok to do that manually, but I did not find a command for this.\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nExample using sonme python file (with multiple function definitions \"def my_func...()\"\r\n\r\n- Start a macro, e.g. with qq\r\n- use \"/def \" to search for \"def \"\r\n- esc to normal mode\r\n- w to go to start of function name\r\n- i to go into insert mode, insert some new prefix to be used for all functions\r\n- esc to normal mode\r\n- j to move down\r\n- q to end macro\r\n\r\nNow rerun the macro with @q and @@, instead of inserting at each occurrence the text get's inserted at arbitrary locations since the animation actually seems to emulated key strokes.\r\n \r\nOf course this is a contrived example and could be replaced by `:%s /def /def prefix/g` or similar.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\ntext gets inserted at every function definition\n\n### Actual behavior\n\ntext get's inserted at arbitrary locations since the animation actually seems to emulated key strokes\r\n",
