            "body": "> This might be difficult to fix, however it would be nicht to just temporarily deactivate animation while running a macro. It would be ok to do that manually, but I did not find a command for this.\r\n\r\nIn would indeed be not quite easy to do automatically when running macro as there seems to be no event triggering to hook into.\r\n\r\nDid you try `:lua MiniAnimate.config.scroll.enable = false`? And then later `:lua MiniAnimate.config.scroll.enable = true`.\r\n\r\nYou can also create a mapping to toggle that with `'<Cmd>lua MiniAnimate.config.scroll.enable = not MiniAnimate.config.scroll.enable<CR>'` as right hand side.",
